---
import ToolingLayout from "../../layouts/ToolingLayout.astro";
import { WarningText } from "@i-dot-ai-npm/component-library-astro";
---

<ToolingLayout
  title="Policies and processes"
  currentPath="/tooling/policies-and-processes"
>
  <h1 class="govuk-heading-xl">Policies and processes</h1>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    These policies explain how you should use the Gateway, and how to ask for
    help:
  </p>

  <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="#acceptable-use">
        acceptable use of the Gateway
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="#managing-access-keys">
        managing access keys
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="#budgets">
        budgets for keys
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="#rates-and-limits">
        rates and limits
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="#uptime-and-reliability">
        uptime and reliability
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="#external-users">
        access for external users
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="#getting-access-to-models">
        getting access to models
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="#sharing-data">
        sharing data with models
      </a>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-m" id="acceptable-use">
    Acceptable use of the Gateway
  </h2>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    You should only access AI models through the gateway (including Bedrock
    models). Find out more about{" "}
    <a class="govuk-link" href="#getting-access-to-models">
      model access and adding models
    </a>
    .
  </p>

  <p class="govuk-body">You may only use the Gateway for:</p>

  <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>exploration (investigating AI products and capabilities)</li>
    <li>
      product development (prototyping, building, maintaining, and evaluation)
    </li>
    <li>
      personal business use (for example, performance or professional
      development)
    </li>
  </ul>

  <WarningText>
    Do not use AI outputs as the sole basis for decisions affecting individuals,
    without human review or rigorous evaluation. You must comply with the{" "}
    <a
      class="govuk-link"
      href="https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/civil-service-code/the-civil-service-code"
    >
      Civil Service Code
    </a>
    . Breach of this policy will be handled under the DSIT disciplinary process.
  </WarningText>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-m" id="managing-access-keys">
    Managing access keys
  </h2>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    There are{" "}
    <a
      class="govuk-link"
      href="https://docs.litellm.ai/docs/proxy/access_control#when-to-use-each-key-type"
    >
      3 kinds of key
    </a>
    :
  </p>

  <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>
      <strong>User</strong>: for your personal use (for example, performance or
      development)
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Product</strong>: for the product or app to use directly
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Team</strong>: for work with teams (such as Consult), professions
      (for community work) or functions (for evaluation)
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="govuk-heading-s" id="creating-keys">
    Creating personal AI gateway keys
  </h3>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    You can create personal AI gateway keys in 3 ways depending on if the model
    is available. You can{" "}
    <a class="govuk-link" href="https://llm-gateway-console.i.ai.gov.uk/models">
      see available models
    </a>
    .
  </p>

  <p class="govuk-body">If the model is:</p>

  <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>
      available through an approved provider, use the Gateway app to{" "}
      <a
        class="govuk-link"
        href="https://llm-gateway-console.i.ai.gov.uk/keys/generate/personal"
      >
        create a personal key
      </a>{" "}
      or{" "}
      <a
        class="govuk-link"
        href="https://llm-gateway-console.i.ai.gov.uk/keys/generate/team"
      >
        create a team key
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      available with a provider key, contact us in the #ai-model-gateway-team
      channel on i.AI Slack for a unique provider key
    </li>
    <li>
      not available, raise a PR for a new provider and model explaining why you
      need to use it - SLT will review and grant a provider key on a
      case-by-case basis
    </li>
  </ul>

  <WarningText>
    You must only access models using your own keys. You must not share your
    key.
  </WarningText>

  <h4 class="govuk-heading-s">Creating temporary keys</h4>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    If someone outside i.AI needs a key for a short time (like a hackathon for 2
    days), contact us in the #ai-model-gateway-team channel to request a
    temporary key.
  </p>

  <h4 class="govuk-heading-s">Key rotation</h4>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Your user and team keys will expire every 2 months, and you will need to
    update them.
  </p>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    This keeps them secure and helps you make sure every key is still needed
    (for example, processes you don't need any more).
  </p>

  <h4 class="govuk-heading-s">Support with keys</h4>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Contact us in the #ai-model-gateway-team channel, if:
  </p>

  <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>your team doesn't exist</li>
    <li>you need a product key</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    We will review and meet your request within 3 working days.
  </p>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-m" id="budgets">
    Budgets for keys
  </h2>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Spend controls are applied using role-based access controls for the 3 kinds
    of key. There are 3 proposed monthly budget limits, a:
  </p>

  <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>personal budget for each user</li>
    <li>team budget for each person in a product team</li>
    <li>budget for each product</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    You can see your remaining budget on{" "}
    <a class="govuk-link" href="https://llm-gateway-console.i.ai.gov.uk/">
      your summary page in the AI Gateway app
    </a>
    .
  </p>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Contact us in the #ai-model-gateway-team channel to request a temporary or
    permanent increase to your budget. Gateway management will review and
    approve this within 1 working day.
  </p>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-m" id="rates-and-limits">
    Rates and limits
  </h2>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    There are limits on how much of the model's capacity any one user can use.
    This stops anyone blocking everyone else during busy periods. You can see
    your limits on{" "}
    <a class="govuk-link" href="https://llm-gateway-console.i.ai.gov.uk/">
      your summary page in the AI Gateway app
    </a>
    .
  </p>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    If you're hitting limits and it's affecting your work, contact us in the
    #ai-model-gateway-team channel.
  </p>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-m" id="uptime-and-reliability">
    Uptime and reliability
  </h2>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    You should report outages as soon as you identify them. Contact us in the
    #ai-model-gateway-team channel and we will update you when it's resolved.
  </p>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-m" id="external-users">
    Gateway access for external users
  </h2>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    All i.AI employees are allowed access to the Gateway.
  </p>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    If you are not an i.AI employee, you may be able to get network access (IP
    allowlisting). Contact us in the #ai-model-gateway-team channel with your
    static IP range.
  </p>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-m" id="getting-access-to-models">
    Getting access to models
  </h2>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Check{" "}
    <a class="govuk-link" href="https://llm-gateway-console.i.ai.gov.uk/models">
      available models
    </a>{" "}
    to see which models you can use. All models listed are approved and
    accessible using the LLM gateway.
  </p>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    If the model is not in the list, you can add a model:
  </p>

  <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>
      immediately, if it is from an approved provider (such as Azure, Bedrock
      and GCP) by raising a pull request
    </li>
    <li>
      with SLT approval, if it is from a new provider (email a member of SLT
      explaining why you need to use it)
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Contact us in the #ai-model-gateway-team channel to discuss getting access
    to an 'unavailable' model.
  </p>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-m" id="sharing-data">
    Sharing data with models (information security)
  </h2>

  <p class="govuk-body">If the model is not cleared for:</p>

  <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>
      official-sensitive data, you must not share any information marked as
      official-sensitive or above
    </li>
    <li>
      personal identifiable information, you must anonymise and remove personal
      identifiers from data before using it with any model
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    If you are unsure if data is suitable for use with a model, contact us in
    the #ai-model-gateway-team channel.
  </p>

  <WarningText>
    If you accidentally share inappropriate information with a model you think
    you shouldn't have (a data breach), email a member of SLT. They will review
    the breach and support you to fix any issues and may do a post-incident
    report so that lessons can be learned.
  </WarningText>
</ToolingLayout>
